    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166-a2">

                <pb facs="0603" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v44p1/pg572"/>


                <head>Draft Press Statement Prepared in the National Security Council<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d166-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian">undated</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Draft Press Statement</hi></p>
                <p>“The 131st B–52 bomber to be equipped to carry air-launched cruise missiles
                    completed its conversion today. By this action the United States passed out of
                    technical observance of SALT II. This step reflects the President’s May 27, 1986
                    decision that current and future decisions reflecting our strategic forces must
                    be based on overall U.S. military requirements and the threat we face.</p>
                <p>“After a few days of additional testing, the bomber involved will return to its
                    operational base at Carswell Air Force Base, Texas.”</p>
            </div>
